('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Economics', 'hard', 7.5, 'According to the passage, what criticism is made of a truly universal (rather than targeted) basic income scheme?', '23000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', null, '["It is considered an inefficient use of public funds because payments also go to wealthy citizens who do not need them","It increases the administrative burden compared with means-tested welfare","It has been shown to always reduce labour force participation","It is currently illegal in most countries that have considered it"]', '"It is considered an inefficient use of public funds because payments also go to wealthy citizens who do not need them"', 'The passage states some critics see "a truly universal payment, one distributed even to wealthy citizens who do not need it," as "an inefficient use of limited public funds."', 'This criticism is specifically about universality, distinguishing it from the general cost objection raised earlier in the passage.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 70, 8, false),
