('reading', 'yes_no_not_given', 'Economics', 'hard', 7, 'Most pilot programmes found that recipients almost entirely stopped working once they began receiving payments.', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"NO"', 'The passage states "most pilots have found only modest reductions in overall hours worked" and that "overall employment rates... have in most studied cases remained largely stable," contradicting the claim of near-total withdrawal from work.', 'The word "modest" in the passage directly contradicts the extreme claim "almost entirely stopped working."', '{"yes_no_not_given"}', 70, 3, false),
('reading', 'yes_no_not_given', 'Economics', 'hard', 7.5, 'The first pilot programme testing universal basic income took place in a Nordic country during the 1970s.', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"NOT GIVEN"', 'The passage mentions pilots conducted in "wealthy Nordic economies" among other locations, but gives no date for when this occurred or which pilot was first.', 'The passage names a region but never gives a specific decade or claims a particular pilot was the first — do not assume a date that is not stated.', '{"yes_no_not_given"}', 65, 4, false),
('reading', 'yes_no_not_given', 'Economics', 'hard', 7.5, 'All economists agree that paying a universal benefit to every adult is a more efficient use of public funds than a targeted alternative.', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"NO"', 'The passage states "some economists argue" a universal payment is inefficient compared with targeting, while "UBI''s defenders counter" with their own arguments — meaning economists are divided, not unanimous, and the passage does not claim universal payment is more efficient.', 'The presence of two opposing camps ("some economists" versus "defenders") rules out any claim of unanimous agreement.', '{"yes_no_not_given"}', 75, 5, false),
('reading', 'matching_features', 'Economics', 'hard', 7, 'Match the claim to the group most closely associated with making it: ''A universal payment would remove the disincentive created by phased benefit withdrawal.''', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Advocates of UBI","Critics of UBI","Researchers evaluating pilots"]', '"Advocates of UBI"', 'The passage attributes this claim to "proponents," who argue a universal payment "would eliminate this disincentive entirely."', 'The word "proponents" is a direct synonym for "advocates" — match the paraphrase to identify the correct group.', '{"matching_features"}', 70, 6, false),
('reading', 'matching_features', 'Economics', 'hard', 7, 'Match the claim to the group most closely associated with making it: ''Pilot programmes typically offer payments only for a short, fixed period, which limits what they reveal about a permanent scheme.''', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Advocates of UBI","Critics of UBI","Researchers evaluating pilots"]', '"Critics of UBI"', 'The passage attributes this argument to "critics," who "contend that behaviour observed under these conditions may differ considerably from how people would respond to a genuinely permanent, nationwide scheme."', 'Look for the paragraph beginning "Critics of UBI, however, argue" and identify the claim that follows it.', '{"matching_features"}', 70, 7, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Economics', 'medium', 6.5, 'According to the passage, which groups were most likely to reduce their paid working hours after receiving UBI payments in pilot studies?', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Retired people and the unemployed","Parents of young children and full-time students","Factory workers and the self-employed","Recipients living only in sub-Saharan Africa"]', '"Parents of young children and full-time students"', 'The passage states reductions were "concentrated disproportionately among specific groups, such as parents of young children and full-time students."', 'The passage names these two groups explicitly — avoid options describing groups not mentioned in this context.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 65, 8, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Economics', 'medium', 6.5, 'What psychological benefit did several pilot studies report among recipients?', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["Increased ambition to change careers entirely","Reduced stress and improved life satisfaction","Greater interest in local politics","Higher rates of homeownership"]', '"Reduced stress and improved life satisfaction"', 'The passage states studies reported "measurable improvements in self-reported stress levels... and general life satisfaction" among recipients.', 'Focus on paragraph 4, which lists the specific psychological and wellbeing outcomes measured.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 65, 9, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Economics', 'hard', 7, 'What is a negative income tax, as described in the passage?', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, '["A tax refund available only to high earners","A scheme in which payments are gradually withdrawn as a recipient''s own earned income rises","A one-time payment made only during economic recessions","A special tax imposed only on companies that automate jobs"]', '"A scheme in which payments are gradually withdrawn as a recipient''s own earned income rises"', 'The passage defines a negative income tax as one "under which payments are gradually withdrawn as a recipient''s separate earned income rises."', 'This definition appears in paragraph 6, contrasted directly with genuine universal basic income.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 70, 10, false),
('reading', 'table_completion', 'Economics', 'hard', 7, 'Complete the table using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS. Policy: Negative income tax — Key feature: payments are gradually ______ as earned income rises.', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"withdrawn"', 'The passage states payments under a negative income tax "are gradually withdrawn as a recipient''s separate earned income rises."', 'The completion word is the verb describing what happens to the payment as income rises — locate it directly in the definition sentence.', '{"table_completion"}', 60, 11, false),
('reading', 'table_completion', 'Economics', 'hard', 7, 'Complete the table using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS. Policy: Targeted cash-transfer programmes — Key feature: restricted to specific ______ populations.', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"low-income"', 'The passage describes "more narrowly targeted cash-transfer programmes restricted to specific low-income populations."', 'Search paragraph 6 for the word "restricted," which introduces the completion phrase directly.', '{"table_completion"}', 60, 12, false),
('reading', 'table_completion', 'Economics', 'hard', 7, 'Complete the table using NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS. Policy: Genuine UBI — Key feature: eligibility does not depend on proving ______, unlike means-tested welfare.', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', null, null, '"need"', 'The passage states means-tested welfare systems require "recipients to prove need," a requirement UBI, being unconditional, removes entirely.', 'This links back to paragraph 2''s description of means-tested systems, which UBI is defined in contrast to.', '{"table_completion"}', 60, 13, false),
