('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Culture & Economics', 'medium', 6.5, 'Which paragraph discusses backlogs in vinyl production caused by limited pressing plant capacity?', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["Paragraph 1: The historical decline and recent resurgence of vinyl sales","Paragraph 2: The tactile and visual appeal of vinyl records","Paragraph 3: The unresolved debate about vinyl''s sound quality","Paragraph 4: Manufacturing bottlenecks in the vinyl industry","Paragraph 5: Vinyl as a revenue source for musicians","Paragraph 6: The demographics and symbolic meaning of vinyl buying"]', '"Paragraph 4: Manufacturing bottlenecks in the vinyl industry"', 'Paragraph 4 describes how shrunken pressing capacity has "led to lengthy production backlogs, sometimes stretching to many months."', 'The word "bottleneck" in the paragraph is a strong signal matching the question''s focus on production backlogs.', '{"matching_headings"}', 65, 5, false),
('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Culture & Economics', 'medium', 6.5, 'Which paragraph explains why buying a physical record engages the listener differently from streaming a song?', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["Paragraph 1: The historical decline and recent resurgence of vinyl sales","Paragraph 2: The tactile and visual appeal of vinyl records","Paragraph 3: The unresolved debate about vinyl''s sound quality","Paragraph 4: Manufacturing bottlenecks in the vinyl industry","Paragraph 5: Vinyl as a revenue source for musicians","Paragraph 6: The demographics and symbolic meaning of vinyl buying"]', '"Paragraph 2: The tactile and visual appeal of vinyl records"', 'Paragraph 2 contrasts the "tactile, deliberate nature of the vinyl listening experience" with "streaming a song with a single tap."', 'Look for the paragraph directly comparing a physical action (removing a record, placing a needle) with a digital action (tapping a screen).', '{"matching_headings"}', 65, 6, false),
('reading', 'matching_headings', 'Culture & Economics', 'medium', 6.5, 'Which paragraph discusses buyers who do not own equipment capable of playing the records they purchase?', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["Paragraph 1: The historical decline and recent resurgence of vinyl sales","Paragraph 2: The tactile and visual appeal of vinyl records","Paragraph 3: The unresolved debate about vinyl''s sound quality","Paragraph 4: Manufacturing bottlenecks in the vinyl industry","Paragraph 5: Vinyl as a revenue source for musicians","Paragraph 6: The demographics and symbolic meaning of vinyl buying"]', '"Paragraph 6: The demographics and symbolic meaning of vinyl buying"', 'Paragraph 6 states many younger buyers "do not even own a functioning record player, purchasing vinyl instead primarily as a collectible object."', 'This is the final paragraph, which shifts focus to who is buying vinyl and why, rather than how it is made or sounds.', '{"matching_headings"}', 65, 7, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Culture & Economics', 'medium', 6.5, 'According to the passage, why do independent labels sometimes struggle to get their records pressed quickly?', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["They lack sufficient funds to pay pressing plants at all","Pressing plants often prioritise large-scale reissues from major labels","Independent labels are legally restricted from using vinyl","Vinyl pressing plants only accept orders from major labels"]', '"Pressing plants often prioritise large-scale reissues from major labels"', 'The passage states independent labels compete "against major record labels commissioning large-scale reissues... releases that pressing plants often prioritise because of their higher guaranteed sales volume."', 'Eliminate the absolute options ("only," "legally restricted") which the passage does not support.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 65, 8, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Culture & Economics', 'medium', 6.5, 'Why has vinyl become an important source of income for many musicians, according to the passage?', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["Streaming royalties are typically calculated as a very small fraction per play","Vinyl records are exempt from sales tax in most countries","Touring has become significantly less profitable than in the past","Vinyl records cost less to manufacture than compact discs"]', '"Streaming royalties are typically calculated as a very small fraction per play"', 'The passage states "royalty payments from streaming services are typically calculated as a fraction of a cent per individual play," making vinyl a more significant direct revenue source by comparison.', 'Focus on paragraph 5''s direct explanation of streaming royalties before it introduces vinyl as a comparison.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 65, 9, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Culture & Economics', 'hard', 7, 'What does the passage suggest about the relationship between many young vinyl buyers and the format?', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', null, '["They primarily buy vinyl to achieve genuinely superior sound quality","They often buy records without owning a device capable of playing them","They mostly buy vinyl second-hand from established collectors","They buy vinyl exclusively to listen to classical music"]', '"They often buy records without owning a device capable of playing them"', 'The passage states many young buyers "do not even own a functioning record player, purchasing vinyl instead primarily as a collectible object."', 'This is one of the passage''s more surprising claims, explicitly flagged as "striking to industry observers."', '{"multiple_choice"}', 70, 10, false),
