('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Agriculture', 'medium', 6.5, 'According to the passage, what triggers the transformation of desert locusts from a solitary to a gregarious form?', '24000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, '["Exposure to unusually high temperatures","Repeated physical contact between individuals at high population density","A sudden shortage of available vegetation","Migration across an international border"]', '"Repeated physical contact between individuals at high population density"', 'The passage states that when populations become dense, "repeated physical contact between individuals triggers a cascade of hormonal and neurological changes."', 'The trigger is physical contact resulting from density, not the rainfall itself, which only creates the conditions for density to build.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 65, 7, false),
