('reading', 'short_answer', 'Science', 'medium', 6, 'What term do psychologists use for the theory that a rapid brain system judges familiarity based on overlapping features?', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '["familiarity without recollection","\"familiarity without recollection\""]', 'The passage introduces the term directly: "One of the leading explanations centres on what psychologists call familiarity without recollection."', 'Terms placed in quotation marks in academic-style passages are usually the exact answer expected for a short-answer question about terminology.', '{"short_answer"}', 55, 7, false),
('reading', 'multiple_choice', 'Science', 'medium', 6, 'According to the passage, what happens when doctors electrically stimulate the rhinal cortex in some epilepsy patients?', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, '["Patients lose consciousness immediately","Patients often report a sensation of déjà vu","Patients experience improved long-term memory","Patients report a decrease in seizure frequency"]', '"Patients often report a sensation of déjà vu"', 'The passage states stimulating the rhinal cortex "has in some cases reliably reproduced the sensation of déjà vu in fully conscious patients," which also rules out loss of consciousness.', 'Note the passage says patients remain "fully conscious" during stimulation, which directly eliminates the option about losing consciousness.', '{"multiple_choice"}', 65, 8, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Science', 'hard', 6.5, 'Doctors are certain that déjà vu is caused by an actual memory being retrieved from long ago.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states déjà vu "results not from an actual, if buried, memory being retrieved, but from a kind of false alarm," which contradicts the statement.', 'The structure "not from X, but from Y" clearly rules out X as the accepted explanation, so treat X-based statements as false.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 60, 9, false),
('reading', 'summary_completion', 'Science', 'hard', 6.5, 'Complete the summary using NO MORE THAN ONE WORD: According to the dual-process model, ______ is a fast, automatic sense that something has been encountered before, while recollection retrieves specific contextual details.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"familiarity"', 'The passage defines "familiarity, a fast and relatively automatic gut feeling that something has been encountered before," as distinct from recollection.', 'The summary sentence mirrors the passage almost exactly, so the missing word is simply the term being contrasted with "recollection."', '{"summary_completion"}', 55, 10, false),
('reading', 'summary_completion', 'Science', 'hard', 6.5, 'Complete the summary using NO MORE THAN ONE WORD: Déjà vu may occur when the familiarity system fires strongly but the ______ system retrieves nothing.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"recollection"', 'The passage states déjà vu "may represent a rare instance in which the familiarity system fires with unusual strength while the recollection system finds nothing to retrieve."', 'Since "familiarity" is already given, the missing word must be the other of the two processes named in the dual-process model.', '{"summary_completion"}', 50, 11, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Science', 'medium', 6, 'Besides tiredness and frequent travel, what other factor does the passage mention as correlated with déjà vu frequency?', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '["stress","elevated stress"]', 'The passage lists "correlations between déjà vu frequency and factors such as tiredness, elevated stress, and frequent travel to unfamiliar places."', 'When a question gives you two of three items from a list, scan for the sentence containing all of them and identify the missing item.', '{"short_answer"}', 50, 12, false),
('reading', 'true_false_not_given', 'Science', 'hard', 6.5, 'Lab-induced déjà vu experiences are, in every respect, identical to spontaneous déjà vu.', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '"FALSE"', 'The passage states these lab-induced experiences "may not be identical in every respect to spontaneous, naturally occurring déjà vu," directly contradicting the claim.', 'The phrase "may not be identical in every respect" is a direct negation of the absolute claim "in every respect... identical" in the statement.', '{"true_false_not_given"}', 55, 13, false),
('reading', 'short_answer', 'Science', 'medium', 6, 'According to the final paragraph, understanding déjà vu''s mechanics could eventually help with the study of what kind of conditions?', '22000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000006', null, null, '["memory disturbances","more serious memory disturbances","chronic déjà vu"]', 'The final paragraph states understanding the mechanism "could eventually inform the study of more serious and persistent memory disturbances, including rare conditions in which patients experience chronic, near-constant feelings of déjà vu."', 'The concluding paragraph of a passage often generalises from the specific topic to a broader field of application — check the final sentences for this kind of forward-looking claim.', '{"short_answer"}', 55, 14, false),
